{"@context":["https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/ns/content/v1.jsonld",{"@base":"https://litlfred.github.io/folio/","folio-assistant-sci":"https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant-sci/v0/ns/"}],"@id":"papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/def-spatial-realization-functor","@type":["folio-assistant-sci:Definition","doco:Section"],"label":"def:spatial-realization-functor","kind":"definition","title":"Spatial realization functor","uses":["papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/def-categorical-point","papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/def-frobenius-pairing","papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/def-categorical-reeb"],"tags":["spectrum","functor","contact-geometry"],"leanRef":"qou:QOU.SpatialRealizationFunctor","text":"spatial-realization-functor.md","leanSource":"spatial-realization-functor.lean","provenance":"authored","html":"<a id=\"def:spatial-realization-functor\"></a><p>Let <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">(\\mathbf{C}, A, \\tau)</code> be a quantum observable universe. The <strong>spatial realization</strong> of <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">A</code> is the space</p>\n<pre><code class=\"language-math math-display\">  M = \\mathrm{Spec}(A) = \\{ p \\colon \\mathbf{1} \\to A \\mid\n  p \\text{ is a categorical point} \\},</code></pre>\n<p>equipped with the following structures in <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\mathbf{C}</code>:</p>\n<ol>\n<li>for each point <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">p</code>, the <strong>augmentation ideal</strong> <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\mathfrak{m}_p = \\ker(p^* \\colon A \\to \\mathbf{1})</code>;</li>\n<li>the <strong>contact form</strong> <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\varTheta_A \\in \\Omega^1(A)</code>, induced by the Frobenius form <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\int_A \\colon A \\to \\mathbf{1}</code> via pullback along the universal derivation <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">d \\colon A \\to \\Omega^1(A)</code>;</li>\n<li>the <strong>Reeb derivation</strong> <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\xi</code>, the generator of the maximal torus action.</li>\n</ol>\n","source":"folio/quantum-observable-universe/models-of-qous/spatial-realization-functor.md","heading":"Definition","number":"5.6.3","page":"b/def-spatial-realization-functor","qa":{"counts":{"pass":82,"fail":0,"warn":1,"na":9,"unknown":0,"stale":66},"milnor":{"total":3,"notPassing":0}},"lean":{"expected":true,"ref":"qou:QOU.SpatialRealizationFunctor","via":"sibling","path":"folio/quantum-observable-universe/models-of-qous/spatial-realization-functor.lean","compiles":"unchecked","sorry":false,"sorryBasis":"text"}}
